    "title": "Texas A&M vs Texas game score: Aggies take Game 1 over Longhorns",
    "text": "COLLEGE STATION — In a game with five lead changes and a late-inning surge Friday, Texas A&M baseball outlasted Texas to take Game 1, 9-8.The Longhorns (27-6, 9-4 SEC) entered the ninth trailing by three, then blasted two solo home runs. However, Aggies (26-7, 8-5) reliever Clayton Freshcorn settled down to retire the final batter and recorded the three-inning save.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢A&M used six runs in the final four innings to help secure the win.Texas A&M outfielder Caden Sorrell celebrates while rounding second base against Tennessee Tech on Feb. 13, 2026 at Blue Bell Park in College Station. Cooper Daniels/Cooper Daniels/Texas A&M AthleticsThe Aggies tallied seven hits, highlighted by first baseman Gavin Grahovac going 2-for-4 with a double and a triple. The Longhorns scraped to 10 hits with Aiden Robbins collecting three and hitting two home runs.Article continues below this adThe two teams used eight pitchers in the outing, with Texas using four relievers, as the in-state rivals traded blows throughout the night.Aggies junior Shane Sdao had a solid night with strikeouts, but left the outing on the hook for the loss. The left-hander pitched four innings, gave up four runs and five hits and walked three on 90 pitches.Longhorns’ starting pitcher, Ruger Riojas, had an up-and-down night. The righty lasted five innings, giving up four runs and five hits. He struck out four and allowed two walks on 83 pitches.Article continues below this adNext up for the Aggies is 2 p.m. Saturday as they turn to right-hander Aiden Moss to take the series.Final updates from the action: Texas A&M baseball vs Texas: Scoring updates from Friday Final: Texas A&M 9, Texas 8 End 8: Texas A&M 9, Texas 6 Sorrell slapped a two-out single to right field, leading to a high chopper to third base by Hacopian that was an E5 and drove in another insurance run for the Aggies.Article continues below this ad Mid 8: Texas A&M 8, Texas 6 A 1-2-3 inning for Freshcorn and the Aggies as the A&M pitcher is fired up coming off the mound following striking out two and inducing a foul ball popout. End 7: Texas A&M 8, Texas 6 Duer worked a one-out walk before Partida slapped a single through the right side. Kiel was then hit in the face with a pitch to load the bases with one out.Article continues below this adFrom there, the Longhorns turned to left-handed reliever Ethan Walker. Wilson then ripped a loud out to left field that pushed across the Aggies' eighth run. Texas once again went to the bullpen, bringing in right-hander Max Grubbs. Mid 7: Texas A&M 7, Texas 6 Pack started the inning with a single to center field. From there, Freschcorn struck out Borba and then popped up Becerra. Larson then flew out to center to end the frame. End 6: Texas A&M 7, Texas 6 Duer worked a leadoff walk that ended Riojas's night. Texas turned to reliever Haiden Leffew. A passed ball advanced Duer to second, followed by a Partida walk to put two on. Kiel advanced both with a bunt down the third base line. Wilson then walked to load the bases, followed by Harrison drawing a four-pitch walk to drive in a run.Article continues below this adThe Longhorns then turned to right-hand reliever Brett Crossland, who proceeded to walk Kellner to tie the game. From there, Grahovac lifted a sac fly to right field to give the Aggies the lead 7-6. Mid 6: Texas 6, Texas A&M 4 Duplantier led off the inning with a softly hit single that he legged out. Presley Courville pinch hit for Livingston and laid down a sacrifice bunt to advance the runner to second. A dribbler to first by Mendoza pushed Duplantier to third with two outs. From there, Tinney hit a two-run home run to right field on a line that just got over the short fence. End 5: Texas A&M 4, Texas 4 A one-out triple by Grahovac led to Sorrell grounding out to second and driving in the tying run.Article continues below this ad Mid 5: Texas 4, Texas A&M 3 A Tinney walk led to a two-run home run by Robbins to right field, giving the Longhorns the lead back. The blast chased Sdao from the game, and the Aggies turned to left-handed reliever Ethan Darden to get them out of the frame. End 4: Texas A&M 3, Texas 2 Partida led off the inning with a home run to left field to give the Aggies back the lead.Article continues below this ad Mid 4: Texas A&M 2, Texas 2 A bloop single with one out by Larson was followed by Duplantier getting on with a fielder's choice. From there, Livingston doubled down the right field line and drove him home to tie the game at 2-2. End 3: Texas A&M 2, Texas 1 Longhorns right fielder Duplantier lost a Kellner fly ball in the lights, and as a result, the Aggies' shortstop was able to leg out a lead-off triple. Grahovac then proceeded to slap a double on the next pitch to drive him home to tie the game. A passed ball pushed Grahovac to third, allowing Sorrell to ground out to second base and drive him home.Article continues below this ad Mid 3: Texas 1, Texas A&M 0 Mendoza was hit by a pitch, followed by a Tinney walk and a Robbins single to shallow center field to load the bases with one out. From there, Pack lifted a sac fly to right field to drive in the game's first run. End 2: Texas A&M 0, Texas 0 Duer got on with a bouncing single to the left side, beating the shift to start the inning, before Partida worked a four-pitch walk. From there, Kiel bunted badly, and Riojas fielded it cleanly and threw out the runner headed for third. Wilson then struck out, and Harrison popped out to left to strand two.Article continues below this ad Mid 2: Texas A&M 0, Texas 0 A one-out single was all Texas could muster in the inning as Sdao reached three strikeouts. End 1: Texas A&M 0, Texas 0 Aggies went down 1-2-3, with Grahovac coming three feet short of a leadoff home run to straightaway center field.Article continues below this ad Mid 1: Texas A&M 0, Texas 0 A one-out walk was the only offense the Longhorns recorded in the frame. Texas A&M baseball vs Texas lineups Texas A&M 1B Gavin Grahovac CF Caden Sorrell 2B Chris Hacopian DH Jake Duer 3B Nico Partida LF Terrence Kiel II RF Jorian Wilson C Bear Harrison SS Boston Kellner Article continues below this ad Texas 2B Ethan Mendoza C Carson Tinney CF Aiden Robbins LF Anthony Pack Jr. 3B Casey Borba SS Temo Becerra 1B Ashton Larson RF Jayden Duplantier DH Josh Livingston Texas A&M starting pitcher LHP Shane Sdao (3-2, 5.48 ERA) Texas starting pitcher RHP Ruger Riojas (5-1, 2.74 ERA) Texas A&M baseball vs. Texas: How to watch Friday's game When: 7 p.m. FridayArticle continues below this adWhere: Blue Bell Park, College StationTV/radio: SEC NetworkReach Texas A&M beat reporter Tony Catalina via email at Anthony.Catalina@statesman.com.Article continues below this adGet the hookup and your Horns Up with Longhorns coverage.April 10, 2026Tony Catalina is the Texas A&M beat reporter for the Austin American-Statesman. He is a Heisman Trophy voter from Worcester, Mass., with more than five years of sports reporting experience. He previously worked at SB Nation, Pro Football Network and New England Football Journal, where he covered NFL, college and high school football before joining the Statesman. Before pursuing a career in journalism, Catalina served as a high school football coach in Massachusetts and, in 2016, was a recruiting analyst for the University of Georgia football program under head coach Kirby Smart.",
